---
// Two ways to ride — Guided Drive + Free Roam. Clarity demands the full shape
// of the product. Both are real shipped product (the route player + RoamEngine),
// so featuring Roam is honest and differentiating. The art literally encodes
// "fixed route" (closed loop) vs "wander" (open trail).
import { CAR_BODY_PATH } from '../carBody'
---

<section class="section modes" id="modes">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="modes__head">
      <span class="kicker">Two ways to ride</span>
      <h2 class="title">Pick a route — or just wander.</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="modes__grid">
      <!-- Guided Drive -->
      <article class="mode framed">
        <div class="mode__badge"><span class="badge badge--pine badge--dot">The guided drive</span></div>
        <svg class="mode__art" viewBox="0 0 260 130" aria-hidden="true">
          <ellipse cx="130" cy="65" rx="98" ry="44" fill="none" stroke="var(--track-inactive)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="4 4"></ellipse>
          <!-- ordered stop pips -->
          <g fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.6">
            <circle cx="130" cy="21" r="6"></circle>
            <circle cx="228" cy="65" r="6"></circle>
            <circle cx="130" cy="109" r="6"></circle>
            <circle cx="32" cy="65" r="6"></circle>
          </g>
          <g fill="var(--accent)" font-family="'Overpass Mono', monospace" font-size="7.5" text-anchor="middle">
            <text x="130" y="23.6">1</text>
            <text x="228" y="67.6">2</text>
            <text x="130" y="111.6">3</text>
            <text x="32" y="67.6">4</text>
          </g>
          <!-- car token mid-route -->
          <g transform="translate(176 96) scale(0.82)" style="color:var(--amber)">
            <path d={CAR_BODY_PATH} fill="currentColor"></path>
            <circle cx="10.5" cy="14.4" r="2.8" fill="var(--surface-raised)"></circle>
            <circle cx="25" cy="14.4" r="2.8" fill="var(--surface-raised)"></circle>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <p class="mode__body">
          A narrated route, told end to end. Pick a drive — say, the Emerald Bay run — and the
          Skipper takes you stop to stop: the history, the geology, the tall tales, and a dad joke
          or four. Start to finish, he’s got the wheel-talk covered.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Free Roam -->
      <article class="mode framed">
        <div class="mode__badge">
          <span class="badge badge--teal badge--dot">Free roam</span>
        </div>
        <svg class="mode__art" viewBox="0 0 260 130" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M16 96 C58 96 60 40 100 40 C140 40 150 100 196 92 C224 87 232 56 246 46"
            fill="none" stroke="var(--track-inactive)" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="4 4"></path>
          <!-- scattered POI pins (unordered) -->
          <g fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--water)" stroke-width="1.6">
            <circle cx="64" cy="58" r="5.5"></circle>
            <circle cx="118" cy="34" r="5.5"></circle>
            <circle cx="170" cy="104" r="5.5"></circle>
            <circle cx="224" cy="36" r="5.5"></circle>
          </g>
          <g fill="var(--water)">
            <circle cx="64" cy="58" r="1.7"></circle>
            <circle cx="118" cy="34" r="1.7"></circle>
            <circle cx="170" cy="104" r="1.7"></circle>
            <circle cx="224" cy="36" r="1.7"></circle>
          </g>
          <!-- car token free on the trail -->
          <g transform="translate(122 60) scale(0.82)" style="color:var(--amber)">
            <path d={CAR_BODY_PATH} fill="currentColor"></path>
            <circle cx="10.5" cy="14.4" r="2.8" fill="var(--surface-raised)"></circle>
            <circle cx="25" cy="14.4" r="2.8" fill="var(--surface-raised)"></circle>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <p class="mode__body">
          No route — the Skipper just rides along. Driving Tahoe with no plan? He pipes up about
          whatever you pass — a lake, a landmark, a wide spot in the road with a good story. A
          quiet stretch is a perfectly good drive.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="modes__foot body-dim">
      Same voice both modes. He doesn’t read off a card — every telling is generated fresh for
      your drive.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .modes__head {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
  }
  .modes__head .kicker {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }
  .modes__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .modes__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-2xl);
    }
  }
  .mode {
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    padding: var(--space-2xl);
  }
  .mode__badge {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .mode__art {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: var(--surface-sunken);
    border: var(--border-thin) solid var(--keyline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .mode__body {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
  }
  .modes__foot {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
</style>
